# Shell scripts MUST stay LF.
#
# roomwizard-app-init.sh and disable-steelcase.sh are scp'd byte-for-byte onto
# the device and run by BusyBox sh. A CRLF line ending turns the shebang into
# `#!/bin/sh\r`, which BusyBox rejects with a misleading "no such file or
# directory" - the device then boots to a black screen with no launcher and no
# obvious cause.
#
# This host has core.autocrlf=true set system-wide, so without this file the
# next clone on Windows would silently break the device.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Python helpers are also run on the device / under WSL
*.py text eol=lf

# Device-side config and manifest formats
*.conf text eol=lf
*.app  text eol=lf

# Binary assets - never touch
*.ppm binary
*.raw binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.img binary
*.zip binary
*.dat binary
